    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is an expanded version of the Q3 internal audit report:\n\n**Quality Control and Compliance**\n\n* Petty cash reconciliation at Branch 402 resulted in discrepancies of $12.04 on two occasions in July, which did not reveal any systemic issues. However, this may indicate a need for closer monitoring of cash handling procedures to prevent any potential financial misstatements.\n* One employee failed the annual GDPR training module, with training scheduled for re-run in October to ensure compliance with data protection regulations.\n\n**Physical Security and Risk Management**\n\n* The back door latch at the North American retail branch was reported by staff as \"sticky,\" although it remains operational. A maintenance ticket was submitted for #882 to address this issue at the earliest possible opportunity.\n* Although no hardware damage was reported, server room temperatures were slightly above the optimal range during the heatwave, which may be worth investigating to prevent potential damage to equipment.\n\n**Operational Efficiency and Effectiveness**\n\n* In Transaction Monitoring, 5% of flagged transactions were reviewed within the required 24-hour window, with 95% reviewed within the window. This suggests a need to review and refine the process for efficiently handling high-priority transactions.\n* KYC (Knowledge Your Customer) files had most documentation in order",
      "source": "target",
